# MCP Client — DeepWiki

Two `mcp-connection` sections against [DeepWiki's public MCP server](https://mcp.deepwiki.com/mcp) (Streamable HTTP, no auth) — a real, third-party remote MCP server, so this validates Voiden's MCP client against something it doesn't control. Both tools take a `repoName` in `owner/repo` form.

DeepWiki also exposes a third tool, `ask_question`, deliberately left out of this always-green fixture — its on-demand AI-generated answers regularly take 15s+ server-side (it streams `notifications/message` progress events while it works), and the headless MCP client here failed against it every time in testing rather than waiting it out. See `KNOWN-ISSUES.md` at the repo root for the full repro.

